                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/121.]</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Memorandum of the third meeting.—Extract.]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Wilson</hi>: Pursuant to the notification
                    of the Department the Haitian and Dominican Ministers met at 11:30 today to
                    further discuss the means of arriving at a settlement of their boundary dispute.
                    The entire meeting was consumed in a discussion of three points: (a) Whether or
                    not the Dominican Minister was at fault in so long delaying the present meeting;
                    (b) minutes of the preceding meeting; and (c) the date of the next meeting. * *
                    * After considerable discussion the morning of July 1st was fixed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Doyle.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
